<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I8a9890de7ae8b8436b784ebf1f4517c5b67fc69a" commit="d0e54261011cebfc7d0fdef18826d09e500cd2d4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: Intel: Correct the xmax volume  The xmax volume should be corrected to ARRAY_SIZE(volume_map)-1, otherwise, the xmax value will be mapped to 0 wrongly.  Signed-off-by: Jie Yang &lt;yang.jie@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit c5f0406bdce6eebc9147a54f4be0250618d3a423) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:29929933 TEST=With the whole series applied on Samus, playback/capture works. &quot;Master Playback Volume&quot;/&quot;Mic Capture Volume&quot; works. cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/INT3438:00/bdw-rt5677/System PCM/codec_reg without crash.  Change-Id: I8a9890de7ae8b8436b784ebf1f4517c5b67fc69a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359054 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359054" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/359054/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I3fcdc1f777c58b248ea53f71d4078359018f9b5e" commit="a363f011c0f9c7e63ffadda5923015baf8e366e7" commit_message="BACKPORT: ASoC: Intel: Add stream direction for pcm-module map  A DAI may have 2 streams(playback/capture) and different modules may be needed for them respectively, so we need add a stream direction here, the combination(dai_id + stream) can tell us which module we really need here.  Signed-off-by: Jie Yang &lt;yang.jie@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 98b9c1d2ce59d98d5921bbdca5a6d7fe40b4a384) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:29929933 TEST=With the whole series applied on Samus, playback/capture works. &quot;Master Playback Volume&quot;/&quot;Mic Capture Volume&quot; works. cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/INT3438:00/bdw-rt5677/System PCM/codec_reg without crash.  Conflicts:  sound/soc/intel/sst-haswell-pcm.c * Fixed the hsw_pcm_module_map to keep using DAI 4 as the Capture PCM.   Upstream has merged the Capture PCM to DAI 0 by commit 7bb73cbd073c   (&quot;ASoC: Intel: Move capture PCM pin to PCM0 for Broadwell/Haswell&quot;)   which is not backported to chromeos-3.14 to avoid userspace-visible   changes on the PCM devices. * Context fix in hsw_pcm_prepare  Change-Id: I3fcdc1f777c58b248ea53f71d4078359018f9b5e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359055 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359055" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/359055/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Id7366bf972ee2c2f4dafd43338bf449e3f122caa" commit="9f99f4ebb14c94d726981a05b81f063d2aeafbaf" commit_message="BACKPORT: ASoC: Intel: Split hsw_pcm_data for playback and capture  There may be 2 pcm streams for a same DAI at most, and these 2 streams should have different hsw_pcm_data, e.g. they have different persistent data, so here we need split hsw_pcm_data for playback and capture, to make sure they won't be mixed and keep cleaned.  Signed-off-by: Jie Yang &lt;yang.jie@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Liam Girdwood &lt;liam.r.girdwood@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7ff9d6714a5c97fb448c53aae801af3d529ecb56) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:29929933 TEST=With the whole series applied on Samus, playback/capture works. &quot;Master Playback Volume&quot;/&quot;Mic Capture Volume&quot; works. cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/INT3438:00/bdw-rt5677/System PCM/codec_reg without crash.  Conflicts:  sound/soc/intel/sst-haswell-pcm.c * Fixed the hsw_pcm_module_map to keep using DAI 4 as the Capture PCM.   Upstream has merged the Capture PCM to DAI 0 by commit 7bb73cbd073c   (&quot;ASoC: Intel: Move capture PCM pin to PCM0 for Broadwell/Haswell&quot;)   which is not backported to chromeos-3.14 to avoid userspace-visible   changes on the PCM devices. * Context fix in hsw_pcm_prepare  Change-Id: Id7366bf972ee2c2f4dafd43338bf449e3f122caa Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359056 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359056" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/359056/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I40b6525b70b3949de7d4be9e228f882e5ca4736e" commit="0a834ed4cd80c3f3af25e2e868357fe64f4a4593" commit_message="FROMLIST: ASoC: Intel: Fix conflicting pcm dev drvdata on haswell  soc-core sets the snd_soc_pcm_runtime-&gt;dev drvdata to snd_soc_pcm_runtime in soc_post_component_init, and access it in places like codec_reg_show.  hsw_pcm_open overwrites the drvdata to point to hsw_pcm_data, confusing soc-core, and causing crashes when cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/INT3438:00/.../System PCM/codec_reg  This patch removes the set in hsw_pcm_open since it's no longer used. commit 7ff9d6714a5c (&quot;ASoC: Intel: Split hsw_pcm_data for playback and capture&quot;) already removed all calls to snd_soc_pcm_get_drvdata(rtd).  Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9219967/) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:29929933 TEST=With the whole series applied on Samus, playback/capture works. &quot;Master Playback Volume&quot;/&quot;Mic Capture Volume&quot; works. cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/INT3438:00/bdw-rt5677/System PCM/codec_reg without crash.  Change-Id: I40b6525b70b3949de7d4be9e228f882e5ca4736e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359057 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359057" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/359057/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I25e5dd93c7a85b94074abc7c7355c7cb8092894c" commit="b5c70f802ca1f137eb35410d45c45c663e94efba" commit_message="initial revision for package_to_container, change base_image_util.sh  package_to_container takes a package and generates a minimal root dep (squashfs for now) container. This container can be entered via minijail0, ksanthanam@ should soon have a libcontainer utility ready for the same. Also change build_library/base_image_util.sh to factor out common code with package_to_container.  BUG=chromium:624334 TEST=./package_to_container --package=android-tools --board=cyan --extra=busybox produces android-tools.sqsh with busybox in the same dir.  Change-Id: I25e5dd93c7a85b94074abc7c7355c7cb8092894c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357020 Commit-Ready: Ashish Gaurav &lt;ashishgaurav@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ashish Gaurav &lt;ashishgaurav@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="357020" owner_email="ashishgaurav@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/20/357020/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I49d974921ba7d46022dcc2654640dec29b6368bd" commit="93b3bbfa0acfd7e3a1f324e9a88051f3e250e0f8" commit_message="arc-mesa-img: Unlock/relock mutex in droid_window_dequeue_buffer  Similarly to 1ea233c6f3 &quot;platform_android: prevent deadlock in droid_swap_buffers&quot;, droid_window_dequeue_buffer can also deadlock, so we must release and reacquire the display mutex.  This only seem to happen on Imagination's mesa, which introduces a DRI query buffer extension.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54931 TEST=Swipe photos in Photos TEST=android.textureview.cts.TextureViewTest#testTextureViewStress200Hz      passes  Change-Id: I49d974921ba7d46022dcc2654640dec29b6368bd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358368 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358368" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/68/358368/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie311c3f871ba642ee984e6be3fd2c4e2c370c343" commit="44e8cd1b6a9ae944fec203cba5f52c352c541007" commit_message="sysroot_wrapper: Wunused-local-typedefs is now supported by clang.  This flag is now supported by clang. Need to update the wrapper to avoid removing it when the user has specified it.  BUG=chromium:625067 TEST=Built Simple Chrome with GN and Clang compiler by default.  Change-Id: Ie311c3f871ba642ee984e6be3fd2c4e2c370c343 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358770 Commit-Ready: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Steven Bennetts &lt;stevenjb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="358770" owner_email="llozano@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/70/358770/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If65d86735c10237be73b02a508ffcf2bbe161d9f" commit="9afa897d8f231c75f25044bde48df87f4eb8f848" commit_message="instalog: add batching functionality to input_log_file  To prevent getting stuck on a huge input file, rewrite input_log_file to process batches of N events.  Also, refactor code related to truncating log files, to minimize log file locking time.  BUG=chromium:609069 TEST=Manually on DUT  Change-Id: If65d86735c10237be73b02a508ffcf2bbe161d9f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358337 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chun-ta Lin &lt;itspeter@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358337" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/37/358337/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia5893460e0b29f1945cb2aae45a5f10b08fe1ed1" commit="6adb8f1c10ad6ab4de6290840302807a8506154c" commit_message="tpm2: add nvram lock and hierarchy control commands  The firmware needs to lock the kernel rollback index before starting up the kernel. The TPM2_NV_WriteLock command is used for that.  We also want to limit the amount of control the user space apps have over TPM. With TPM1.2 it was achieved by deasserting physical presence. TPM2 specification allows to achieve the same goal by disabling Platform Hierarchy, which is active out of reset.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50465 TEST=verified that all commands succeed and chrome OS boots up fine.  Change-Id: Ia5893460e0b29f1945cb2aae45a5f10b08fe1ed1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358351 Commit-Ready: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358351" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/51/358351/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8561.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>